// RAG evaluation corpus (K02, issue #32; plan 22 section 7).
//
// EVERY SOURCE BELOW IS SIMULATED. None of it is HUTCH policy, HUTCH terms and
// conditions, or any real regulation, and none of the figures in it is a real
// HUTCH figure (I16). The `source_id` of every entry starts with `SIM-` so that
// a line copied out of this file cannot be mistaken for governed content, and
// the owners are placeholder role names.
//
// REQUIRES HUTCH CONFIRMATION for the real corpus. This set exists to measure
// the retriever, not to answer a customer: what is being measured is whether a
// query finds the clause that is *about* it, which does not depend on the text
// being true.
//
// It is deliberately adversarial in one respect: several entries are about
// neighbouring topics that share vocabulary (pack activation vs pack expiry vs
// pack not working; double charge vs unexpected charge vs refund timing). A
// retriever that merely keyword-matches "pack" ranks all three the same, so the
// set would not distinguish a working retriever from a broken one if every
// topic were unique.
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-FUP", "version": 1, "title": "Fair usage on unlimited packs", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "4.1 An unlimited pack is subject to a fair usage threshold.\n\n4.2 Once the fair usage threshold is reached in a billing cycle, the connection speed may be reduced for the remainder of that cycle.\n\n4.3 The speed returns to normal at the start of the next billing cycle without any action by the subscriber."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-PACK-ACTIVATE", "version": 1, "title": "Activating a data pack", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "7.1 A data pack is activated immediately on successful purchase and a confirmation message is sent.\n\n7.2 Activation may fail where the account balance is insufficient at the moment of purchase, in which case no charge is applied.\n\n7.3 Where activation fails but a charge was applied, the charge is reversed automatically within one billing cycle."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-PACK-EXPIRY", "version": 1, "title": "When a data pack expires", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "8.1 A data pack expires at the end of its stated validity period.\n\n8.2 Any unused allowance remaining in an expired pack lapses and is not carried forward to a new pack.\n\n8.3 Purchasing a new pack of the same type before expiry extends the validity period and the remaining allowance is added."}
{"source_id": "SIM-HELP-PACK-NOT-WORKING", "version": 1, "title": "My pack is active but not working", "kind": "help_article", "owner": "cx-knowledge-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "body": "If a pack shows as active but no data is flowing, the most common cause is that the handset is still holding an old network registration. Restarting the handset forces a fresh registration and resolves most cases. Where the problem persists after a restart, the pack may be scoped to a different connection type than the one in use."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-DOUBLE-CHARGE", "version": 1, "title": "Duplicate charges", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "11.1 Where the same transaction is charged more than once, the duplicate charge is reversed in full.\n\n11.2 A duplicate is identified by an identical amount and merchant within a short window, and the reversal does not require the subscriber to supply evidence.\n\n11.3 The reversal appears as a separate credit entry rather than as an adjustment to the original charge."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-REFUND-TIMING", "version": 1, "title": "How long a refund takes", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "12.1 An approved refund is credited to the account balance within three working days of approval.\n\n12.2 Where the original payment was made by card, the credit may instead be returned to that card, in which case the issuing bank's own timeline applies.\n\n12.3 A refund credited to the account balance is available for immediate use."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-VAS-CONSENT", "version": 1, "title": "Value added service subscriptions", "kind": "vas_rule", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "15.1 A value added service subscription requires the subscriber's explicit consent before the first charge.\n\n15.2 A renewal notification is sent before each renewal charge is applied.\n\n15.3 Where a renewal charge is applied without the required notification, the charge is reversed and the subscription is cancelled."}
{"source_id": "SIM-HELP-RELOAD-MISSING", "version": 1, "title": "My reload has not arrived", "kind": "help_article", "owner": "cx-knowledge-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "body": "A reload normally credits within a few minutes. Where it has not arrived, the most common cause is that the reload was applied to a mistyped connection number. The receipt from the reload point carries the number it was applied to, which is the quickest way to confirm. A reload applied to the wrong number can be traced using the reference on that receipt."}
{"source_id": "SIM-HELP-ESIM", "version": 1, "title": "Setting up an eSIM", "kind": "help_article", "owner": "cx-knowledge-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "body": "An eSIM is installed by scanning the activation code supplied when the profile is issued. The handset must have a working data connection or wifi to download the profile. An activation code can only be used once, so a profile that has been installed and then deleted needs a replacement code before it can be installed again."}
{"source_id": "SIM-HELP-ROAMING", "version": 1, "title": "Using your connection abroad", "kind": "help_article", "owner": "cx-knowledge-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "body": "Roaming must be enabled on the account before travelling. Charges while roaming are set by the visited network and are billed per megabyte unless a roaming pack is active. A roaming pack bought before departure covers data in the destination country for its stated validity."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-SPEND-CAP", "version": 1, "title": "Spending limits and protections", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "19.1 A subscriber may set a monthly spending limit on the account.\n\n19.2 Once the spending limit is reached, further chargeable activity is blocked until the limit is raised or the next billing cycle begins.\n\n19.3 Calls to emergency services and to customer support are never blocked by a spending limit."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-BILLING-CYCLE", "version": 1, "title": "The billing cycle", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "clause_prefix": "T&C", "body": "3.1 The billing cycle begins on the account's own anniversary date each month.\n\n3.2 Allowances that reset monthly do so at the start of the billing cycle and not on the first day of the calendar month.\n\n3.3 A charge is attributed to the cycle in which it was incurred, not the cycle in which it appears on a statement."}
{"source_id": "SIM-HELP-NETWORK-SLOW", "version": 1, "title": "Why is my data slow", "kind": "help_article", "owner": "cx-knowledge-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "en", "body": "Data speed varies with how many connections a cell is serving, so speeds are often lower at busy times of day in dense areas. A sustained drop in one location that does not recover at quiet times usually indicates a fault at the serving cell rather than congestion. Checking the same connection in a different location separates the two."}
{"source_id": "SIM-SOP-REFUND-ESCALATION", "version": 1, "title": "Refund escalation procedure", "kind": "staff_sop", "owner": "cx-operations-sim", "audience": "staff", "language": "en", "body": "A refund above the desk limit is escalated to the duty manager before approval. The duty manager records the justification against the case. Where a subscriber has had more than two refunds in a rolling quarter the case is referred for review before any further refund is approved. The desk limit is not disclosed to subscribers."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-FUP-SI", "version": 1, "title": "සාධාරණ භාවිත ප්රතිපත්තිය", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "si", "clause_prefix": "කොන්දේසි", "body": "4.1 අසීමිත දත්ත පැකේජයක් සාධාරණ භාවිත සීමාවකට යටත් වේ.\n\n4.2 බිල්පත් කාලය තුළ සාධාරණ භාවිත සීමාව ළඟා වූ පසු, එම කාලයේ ඉතිරි කාලය සඳහා සම්බන්ධතාවයේ වේගය අඩු කළ හැකිය.\n\n4.3 ඊළඟ බිල්පත් කාලය ආරම්භයේදී වේගය නැවත සාමාන්ය තත්වයට පත් වේ."}
{"source_id": "SIM-TC-REFUND-TIMING-TA", "version": 1, "title": "பணத்தைத் திரும்பப் பெறும் காலம்", "kind": "legal_text", "owner": "legal-sim", "audience": "customer", "language": "ta", "clause_prefix": "நிபந்தனை", "body": "12.1 அனுமதிக்கப்பட்ட பணத்திரும்பல் அனுமதி வழங்கப்பட்ட மூன்று வேலை நாட்களுக்குள் கணக்கில் வரவு வைக்கப்படும்.\n\n12.2 அசல் கட்டணம் அட்டை மூலம் செலுத்தப்பட்டிருந்தால், அந்த அட்டைக்கே திரும்ப அளிக்கப்படலாம்.\n\n12.3 கணக்கில் வரவு வைக்கப்பட்ட பணத்தை உடனடியாகப் பயன்படுத்தலாம்."}
